__pycache__/
.seen-*
watchdog.jsonl
escalations.jsonl
escalation_queue.jsonl
# ...and the timestamped copies deliver_escalation_answers.py takes before it closes rows.
# They are the same ledger under another name: without this line the backup escapes the rule
# that keeps the ledger out of git, and the first resume that answers anything commits it.
escalation_queue.jsonl.pre-answer.*
escalations.jsonl.pre-answer.*

# Per-replicate divergence collector output. Deliberately NOT committed: it carries the same
# quantities the A/B panel publishes, but under the real replicate ids, so committing it would
# unblind the panel from inside the repo.
.divergence_raw/
# Transcript-growth observations. Runtime state, and per-replicate byte counts are themselves
# a cross-replicate quantity -- they belong beside the other blinded ledgers, not in git.
.transcript_growth.json
